ZED Box Mini carrier: Stereolabs' MB1 pinmux and GPIO settings, as Fjarr's patch to NVIDIA's
two BSD-3-Clause files for them: the P3767 module's HDMI pinmux, which the p3509-a02-p3767-0000
board configuration uses, and the MB1 GPIO file it includes.

spec: docs/32-fleet-ota.md#jetson-test-image ("The board package")

Apply in Linux_for_Tegra/ with `patch -p1 -F0` (no fuzz). The two files are byte-identical in
L4T 36.4.4 and 36.5.2, and this patch applies to both without offset. Its line endings are LF,
as meta-tegra holds the files: its tegra-binaries recipe runs dos2unix on *.dts*. NVIDIA ships
them with CRLF, so on an unconverted tree (jetpack-nixos) either strip the CRs first or apply
the CRLF form that board/check-bct.sh writes to out/board/ (README.md).

The settings are those in Stereolabs' zedbox_mini_device_trees_364.tar
(https://stereolabs.sfo2.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/utils/zed_boxes/zedbox_mini_device_trees_364.tar,
SHA-256 d17993499723bd63c1287bd482400c43322d2b94cf87073654a3daed87c0c03e); the generator
revision comment it also edits stays NVIDIA's. Pinmux, then the MB1 GPIO lists:
- DAP4 (PA4-PA7) leaves I2S4 for GPIO (function rsvd1): PA4, PA6, PA7 pulled down, tristated
  inputs; PA5 driven, input off. The four nodes move from the SFIO to the GPIO part.
- spi1_cs0_pz6: no pull, driven, input off. soc_gpio33_pq6: pulled down, driven.
  soc_gpio39_pn1: driven.
- gpio-input gains A4, A6, A7; gpio-output-low gains A5; gpio-output-high gains Z6 and G6
  (both stay in NVIDIA's gpio-input list too, as Stereolabs ships them).

The patched files keep NVIDIA's copyright notice (2022, NVIDIA CORPORATION & AFFILIATES)
and its BSD-3-Clause licence text.

